{"subjectId":"dsa-basics","id":"dictionary","title":"Dictionary","group":"","order":9,"html":"<p>1. Collection of key-value pairs</p>\n<p>2. Unordered</p>\n<p>3. All keys must be distinct</p>\n<p>4. Values maybe repeated</p>\n<p>5. Uses Hashing internally</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>d = {110 : 'xyz', 101 : 'abc', 105 : 'pqr'}\nprint(d)\n\nd ={}\nd[110] = 'xyz'\nd[101] = 'abc'\nd[105] = 'pqr'\nprint(d)\n\nprint(d.keys())\nprint(d.values())\nprint(d.items())\n\nprint(d[101])\n\nprint(d.get(101))\n\nprint(d.pop(101))\nprint(d)\n\nprint(d.popitem())\nprint(d)</code></pre></figure>"}